  "preamble": "Excrescent [b] arises in a cluster of bilabial nasal plus liquid: as the velum rises before the oral liquid while the lips are still closed, a brief oral bilabial stop is produced. The change is independently attested in Ancient Greek (*amrotos > ámbrotos), Old Spanish (omre > hombre), Old French (numerus > nombre) and Old/Middle English (brǣmel > bræmbel 'bramble').",
